    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution does not autonomously produce binding or signed deliverables; the professional validates.  3.3 Client-file handling support." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk120> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As Legal Agent for Faber IA, I can confirm that Faber IA is committed to maintaining up-to-date social and fiscal obligations, and Faber IA have administrative attestations available." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk121> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding GDPR compliance, Faber IA is familiar with the contractual expectations of clients bound by professional secrecy, which includes respecting confidentiality undertakings." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk122> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Faber IA also have experience working with regulated professions and public-sector clients." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk123> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our platform's intellectual property model is based on proprietary software owned by Faber IA, licensed to the client under a subscription/usage model for the contract term. the client retains full ownership of the client own documents, ingested corpus, and produced data." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk124> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Faber IA provide a reversibility plan that includes the return and deletion of client data at the end of the contract, ensuring compliance with GDPR requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk125> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Faber IA professional liability insurance coverage is 10 million euros per claim, which should mitigate potential risks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk126> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Faber IA also have general civil liability cover and certificates available on request." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk127> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of regulatory compliance, Faber IA maintain Faber IA obligations with a Security & Compliance function and monitor various regulations, including GDPR (including Art. 28 processing agreements), professional secrecy, anti-money-laundering framework (LCB-FT), auditor-independence, and separation-of-duties rules for statutory audit." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk128> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To address the client's requirements: 1. **Explainability and audibility of AI outputs**: Faber IA uses a sovereign European open-weight model under Faber IA open-weight licence and accesses proprietary third-party models under commercial licences with documented terms and supplier dependencies. 2. **No automated decisions without validation**: Faber IA ensure that Faber IA contractual framework does not compromise Faber IA professional obligations, which includes respecting auditor independence and separation of duties. 3. **Anti-money laundering (LCB-FT) compliance**: Faber IA monitors LCB-FT obligations as part of Faber IA regulatory compliance maintenance. 4. **Respect for auditor independence and separation of duties**: Faber IA safeguard professional obligations in our contractual framework to prevent any compromise." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk129> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Potential legal risks that Faber IA should flag include: * Non-compliance with GDPR or other regulatory requirements, which could result in fines or reputational damage. * Breach of confidentiality or professional secrecy, potentially leading to client losses or claims. * Inadequate validation of AI outputs or automated decisions, which may lead to errors or non-compliant actions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "During the handling and review of a client file, the solution must surface relevant information, recall applicable rules, propose a checklist of verifications and flag potential anomalies for human review (e.g. during the révision des comptes). the solution must support the preparation of recurring documents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk130> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on Faber IA company context, Faber IA appear to be generally compliant with the client's requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk131> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, it is essential to conduct a thorough review and ensure that all specific obligations are met throughout the project duration." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk132> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client's global budget is 220,000 over 3 years." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk133> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Annual operating costs must remain controlled and compatible with The client's capacity." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk134> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires a pilot phase followed by progressive rollout." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk135> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on this contract, and are there cost-optimisation strategies our can propose? our normal deal range and financial capacity can accommodate an engagement of €220,000 over 3 years." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk136> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The budget envelope for this contract indicates that one-off project costs should account for 40% of the total budget, which is €88,000, and recurring run costs should account for 60%, which is €132,000, over 3 years." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk137> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our target gross margin range of 25% to 35%, our can estimate our projected revenue from this contract." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk138> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To achieve a gross margin at the lower end of our target gross margin range of 25% to 35% (25%), our cost of goods sold would need to be around €165,000 (€220,000 * (1 - 0.25)), and at the upper end (35%), our cost of goods sold would need to be approximately €143,000 (€220,000 * (1 - 0.35))." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk139> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To optimize costs while maintaining our target gross margin range of 25% to 35%, our could propose a cost-efficient tier for the recurring run costs, such as the sovereign tier with the sovereign European model, which is noted to be the most cost-efficient configuration on the recurring side. propose would help keep the annual operating costs controlled and compatible with the client's capacity." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "No decision or sign-off may be automated.  3.4 Collaboration and mission continuity." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk140> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, by maintaining a three-year cost model that can be re-run if requirements or budgets change, our can ensure flexibility in our pricing strategy and accommodate any adjustments needed during the contract period.  our approach favors cost-efficient tiers/models that protect the gross margin and the predictability of recurring costs, which aligns with the client's requirement for controlled annual operating costs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk141> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By proposing a pilot phase followed by a progressive rollout, as required by The tender, our can further ensure that the solution is well-integrated and cost-effective, thereby optimizing our projected margin on this contract within our target range." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk142> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires an intelligent assistance tool that improves productivity and the quality and reliability of professionals' work while preserving professional secrecy and the reliability of figures. an intelligent assistance tool that improves productivity and the quality and reliability of professionals' work while preserving professional secrecy and the reliability of figures must remain strictly a non-decisional support tool." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk143> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What AI capabilities do we need to develop or integrate to meet these requirements, and what are the potential risks and benefits?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk144> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To meet The client requirements, we can leverage we existing AI capabilities, particularly we Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) approach, which generates answers from passages retrieved from The client controlled corpus. our Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) approach, which generates answers from passages retrieved from the client's controlled corpus ensures that every answer is grounded in validated material, limiting unsupported generation and preserving professional secrecy. our existing AI capabilities include hybrid retrieval, re-ranking, query reformulation, multi-document synthesis, structured extraction with source linking, and template-guided drafting. our existing AI capabilities can be applied to improve productivity and the quality of professionals' work by providing professionals' with accurate and reliable information, assisting in drafting client letters and correspondence, mission notes, file memos, and syntheses." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk145> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure that we tool remains strictly a non-decisional support tool, we will focus on providing information consultation assistance, supporting professionals in professionals daily activities without making decisions or taking actions on professionals behalf. we solution will provide relevant information, recall applicable rules, propose checklists of verifications, and flag potential anomalies for human review." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk146> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The benefits of our Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) approach, which generates answers from passages retrieved from the client's controlled corpus include improved productivity, enhanced quality and reliability of work, and preservation of professional secrecy." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

